        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 26 at 4:08AM EDT until September 27 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...North winds 30 to 40 mph with gusts up to 60 mph.

* WHERE...In Delaware, Delaware Beaches County. In New Jersey,
Eastern Monmouth, Atlantic Coastal Cape May, Coastal Atlantic, and
Coastal Ocean Counties.

* WHEN...Until 6 AM EDT Sunday.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.
Widespread power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult,
especially for high profile vehicles.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind.</instruction>
